# The three binaries CI has to fetch, pinned.
#
# These are the versions CLAUDE.md's Toolchain table names and the versions
# installed on the developer machine — see the repo's working notes. CI must use
# the same ones, and the pin is not cosmetic:
#
#   * Godot 4.7.2 is what project.godot and the export presets declare.
#   * ffmpeg has to be 7 or newer. See the long note at the bottom.
#   * Blender 5.2.2 LTS is load-bearing for
#     test_reproduces_the_committed_meshes_byte_for_byte. The committed
#     assets/machines/*.glb were written by 5.2.2's glTF exporter, and that test
#     compares bytes. A different Blender *fails* it rather than skipping, so
#     floating this version would turn a green suite red for a reason that has
#     nothing to do with the change under test.
#
# The checksums are the publishers' own: Godot's from the release asset,
# Blender's from https://download.blender.org/release/Blender5.2/blender-5.2.2.sha256
#
# Bump a version here and the cache key moves with it, because the key is
# derived from this file's contents.

GODOT_VERSION=4.7.2-stable
GODOT_BINARY=Godot_v4.7.2-stable_linux.x86_64
GODOT_URL=https://github.com/godotengine/godot/releases/download/4.7.2-stable/Godot_v4.7.2-stable_linux.x86_64.zip
GODOT_ZIP_SHA256=cadd3204e728a35d3f13adb7fd0d7902636b79f6b95c40c265eb73b6c35329e4
GODOT_BINARY_SHA256=8d106cbe6144c2dc7e881d61d2429c1a8a76e6b22ef48bd5e48dcf934953f71e

BLENDER_VERSION=5.2.2
BLENDER_DIRNAME=blender-5.2.2-linux-x64
BLENDER_ARCHIVE=blender-5.2.2-linux-x64.tar.xz
BLENDER_SHA256=84098912789dc450e95697c4184fb8a90acbe5111c2ba4aede3fecb57806a168

# download.blender.org sits behind a bot filter that answers some data-centre
# ranges with a 403, so the official host is one candidate among several rather
# than the only one. Tried in order; the checksum above is what decides whether
# the bytes were right, not which host served them.
BLENDER_MIRRORS="https://download.blender.org/release/Blender5.2 https://mirrors.ocf.berkeley.edu/blender/release/Blender5.2 https://ftp.nluug.nl/pub/graphics/blender/release/Blender5.2 https://mirror.clarkson.edu/blender/release/Blender5.2"

# ffmpeg, for tools/assets/wav_to_cue.py's tests. A static build rather than
# `apt-get install ffmpeg`, and this one is not a preference — it is the first
# thing turning CI on actually found.
#
# ubuntu-24.04 ships ffmpeg 6.1.1. On 6.1.1,
# test_a_loop_is_stereo_and_exactly_as_long_as_it_was_told fails: ffmpeg exits 0
# and writes a 0.048-second file where eight seconds were asked for. The cutter's
# loop mode builds a seam with asplit/atrim/asetpts/acrossfade and something in
# that chain behaves differently on 6.x, so the output is silently almost empty
# rather than wrong-and-obvious. Every one of the seven cue-cutting tests passes
# on 8.1.3, and the developer machine's own ffmpeg is a 7.0.2 static build — so
# the audio pipeline has always had a floor of ffmpeg 7 and nothing said so.
#
# Hence a pin: the distro's package is not new enough, and "whatever the runner
# image happens to have" is how this would break again on an image bump.
#
# This is from BtbN/FFmpeg-Builds, which is what ffmpeg.org's own download page
# points Linux users at. The tag is a dated autobuild rather than `latest`,
# because `latest` is a moving pointer and a moving pointer is not a pin.
FFMPEG_VERSION=n8.1.3
FFMPEG_ARCHIVE=ffmpeg-n8.1.3-linux64-gpl-8.1.tar.xz
FFMPEG_URL=https://github.com/BtbN/FFmpeg-Builds/releases/download/autobuild-2026-09-23-14-55/ffmpeg-n8.1.3-linux64-gpl-8.1.tar.xz
FFMPEG_SHA256=8f8d9df68e0b12f401047c244f50ff411f533eb2d306173e73d6a16fb29b320d
FFMPEG_DIRNAME=ffmpeg-n8.1.3-linux64-gpl

# jj (Jujutsu), for tools/assets/tests/test_jj_guard.py.
#
# jj is optional for working in this repo and mandatory for testing it, which is
# the same relationship Blender has with the mesh generator. The licence guard is
# a git pre-commit hook, jj runs no git hooks and has no hook system, so what
# protects a jj commit is the wrapper tools/git/install_hooks.sh puts on PATH —
# and a guard whose tests skip in CI is a guard nobody is checking. Without jj
# installed those nine tests skip, and .github/ci/expected_skips.txt deliberately
# does not list them: CI satisfies the dependency instead.
#
# The musl build, because it is static and runs on any runner image. Checksum is
# of the published release asset.
#
# Installed to $TOOLCHAIN_DIR/jj-$JJ_VERSION/jj and *not* symlinked into
# $TOOLCHAIN_BIN, which is the one place this script's layout deliberately differs
# from the developer machine: there, `jj` on PATH is the guard wrapper, generated
# by tools/git/install_hooks.sh. Putting the bare binary on PATH under the same
# name would be the exact mistake the wrapper exists to prevent.
JJ_VERSION=0.46.0
JJ_ARCHIVE=jj-v0.46.0-x86_64-unknown-linux-musl.tar.gz
JJ_URL=https://github.com/jj-vcs/jj/releases/download/v0.46.0/jj-v0.46.0-x86_64-unknown-linux-musl.tar.gz
JJ_SHA256=fce0271158e665ceb82dc66c5eb95b1728649094e9133074f3b5baece345fc08
